Iris D.: Pushed a small docs PR that standardizes resume token handling + a compact pagination example across Py/TS/Go. URL: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4522
Ben K.: Nice. What's the canonical pattern you're recommending?
Iris D.: Plan: expose a tiny helper in the examples `normalize_resume_token()` that tries base64 decode and falls back to raw string. Show Node/Deno/Py/Go variants and a short pagination cursor usage pattern.
Yara S.: Can you paste the Node + Deno variants? Want to ensure wording is clear for readers copying-paste.
Iris D.: Node:
```js
// Node (commonjs / node):
function decodeResume(token) {
  try {
    return Buffer.from(token, 'base64').toString();
  } catch (e) {
    return token; // already raw
  }
}
```
Deno/browser:
```ts
// Deno / browser:
function decodeResume(token: string) {
  try {
    // atob exists in these runtimes
    return atob(token);
  } catch (e) {
    return token;
  }
}
```
Ben K.: Suggest adding a one-liner: "Only decode when token appears base64 (alphanumeric + /=) to avoid accidental corruption."
Iris D.: Good suggestion. Added a regex check in the helper and documented it.
Yara S.: Python helper?
Iris D.: Python snippet:
```py
import base64
import re

def decode_resume(token: str) -> str:
    if re.match(r'^[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+$', token):
        try:
            return base64.b64decode(token).decode('utf-8')
        except Exception:
            return token
    return token
```
Yara S.: Great. For Go I want to show both decode and passing the cursor in next HTTP request.
Iris D.: Go snippet added — uses `base64.StdEncoding.DecodeString` and checks error. Also shows `context.WithTimeout` and a tiny retry loop for transient stream failures. Kept defaults tiny for readability; called out to increase in prod.
Ben K.: Also add a short paragraph on "token accounting" i.e., partial streamed bytes count once flushed. People keep asking about billing when they resume mid-stream.
Iris D.: Done. Linked to the billing FAQ and clarified that resumed requests may re-send overlapping tokens depending on server semantics.
